# Design Planner credentials — the LLM that reads a brief and plans a room.
#
# Copy this file to .dardesign-llm (gitignored) and fill in ONE of the two
# providers, then restart scripts\run-local-backend.ps1.
#
# UNCONFIGURED IS A WORKING MODE. With no key the planner returns a layout
# computed from DAR's own placement rules and labels it "Planned by DAR's
# rules" in the UI. The demo, the tests and CI all run that path, so nothing
# is dark without a key. The rule path also never claims to have understood
# a culture, a capacity or a colour it did not read.
#
# A Pro/Plus/Max web subscription is NOT API access, for either provider.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option 1 — Google Gemini (free tier)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# aistudio.google.com/apikey issues a key with a free daily quota. Gemini
# enforces `response_schema` with enums, which is what keeps the planner's
# first grounding gate true: an invented catalogue id is unrepresentable.
# Needs: pip install google-genai
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option 2 — Anthropic (pay as you go)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# console.anthropic.com. Used first when both keys are present, because the
# planner's schema was written against its structured outputs.
# Needs: pip install anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional model override. Defaults: gemini-2.5-flash on Gemini,
# claude-sonnet-5 on Anthropic.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DARDESIGN_LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Cost, for the Anthropic path: the catalogue is 27 items, so a plan is
# roughly 1.5k tokens in and 1.5k out — a couple of cents. Repeated briefs are
# served from an in-process cache and cost nothing, the backend refuses more
# than 200 calls per process, and each call's estimated cost is logged.
